Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"78565803f5c0b8ab8684be53e1bfa2a9","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ReeRee[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n There&#039;s tons of makeup tutorial videos on you tube. Check out Makeupgeek and fafinette3x or something like that ... don&#039;t know exact spell..[\/quote] \n \n That&#039;s a great idea. I want to do my own makeup but don&#039;t know where to begin. I don&#039;t want it to just look like my everyday makeup but I also want to still look like myself and I just don&#039;t feel comfortable trusting a complete stranger to get it right.","Attachments":[],"Id":1296435,"PostDate":1285375404,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <br \/> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ReeRee<\/strong>\u00a0<a href='\/forum\/thread\/63963\/doing-your-own-bridal-make-up#post_1433250' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><\/a><br \/> <br \/> <p> There's tons of makeup tutorial videos on you tube. Check out Makeupgeek and fafinette3x or something like that ... don't know exact spell..<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> That's a great idea. I want to do my own makeup but don't know where to begin. I don't want it to just look like my everyday makeup but I also want to still look like myself and I just don't feel comfortable trusting a complete stranger to get it right.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"adcarter41@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1279416320,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230365.jpg?_r=1386538991","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":177,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"adcarter41","Id":230365,"Name":"adcarter41","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6054a07523697af87e1437cd019ab2b6","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I am doing my own make up. I might us a little bit of mac and my Mary Kay products. I am a little worried that I will have to do a lot of test runs, but that okay. haha! I am to scared of paying for someone to do mine and put way to much with colours that I dont like either.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1296474,"PostDate":1285381364,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I am doing my own make up. I might us a little bit of mac and my Mary Kay products. I am a little worried that I will have to do a lot of test runs, but that okay. haha! I am to scared of paying for someone to do mine and put way to much with colours that I dont like either.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"panda_a4@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1254916711,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-222412.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":226,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"loua4","Id":222412,"Name":"loua4","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"560c8ba93bfe387ca76e4c997aefe0cb","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; youtube has tons of videos to give you ideas and instructions.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; another good way to start is going to sephora or favorite makeup counter for a free consult is also good.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; =)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; remember to post pix!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1296790,"PostDate":1285463886,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> youtube has tons of videos to give you ideas and instructions.<\/p> <p> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <p> another good way to start is going to sephora or favorite makeup counter for a free consult is also good.<\/p> <p> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <p> =)<\/p> <p> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <p> remember to post pix!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"wongrose@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1264127439,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-224931.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":133,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"rosieposie","Id":224931,"Name":"rosieposie","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"663a4232fcd36b39dcf87a3e5e64d742","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; check out the video on you tube by Sccastaneda. She does amazing make up tutorial and very easy. She has a few videos on there.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1296828,"PostDate":1285469391,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> check out the video on you tube by Sccastaneda. She does amazing make up tutorial and very easy. She has a few videos on there.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"sheilao_1@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1263513837,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-224684.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"DiamondGirl","Id":224684,"Name":"DiamondGirl","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f65bc8c4df0d8051a86331aa2d98a5ad","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt;I &lt;span style=\"color: black\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\"&gt;would highly recommend going for a makeover at one of your favorite make up counters at a department store or at sephora. You can ask them to explain the techniques that they are using to give you the exact look. Every time I go and buy make up I learn a new tip. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;You can even bring magazine print outs of looks that you&#039;re going for.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"color: black\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\"&gt;I got my make done at sephora for my engagement party and it came out fabulous. They charge you $70 ($50 if you don&#039;t want air brushing) but you get a makeover and a gift card for $70 so you can buy the products that they use on you that day. I thinking about purchasing the air brushing machine that they used on me, its $200 but it makes your skin and complexion look flawless. This is defiantly a must have item if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re doing your make up on your own on your wedding day. I&#039;m still deciding if I&#039;m going to do my make up myself or have it done in Jamaica. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"color: black\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\"&gt;Good luck ladies, hope this info helps. &lt;img alt=\"\" height=\"18\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheers.gif\" title=\"\" width=\"24\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1296841,"PostDate":1285472589,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\">I <span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\">would highly recommend going for a makeover at one of your favorite make up counters at a department store or at sephora. You can ask them to explain the techniques that they are using to give you the exact look. Every time I go and buy make up I learn a new tip. <\/span><\/span><\/span>You can even bring magazine print outs of looks that you're going for.<\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"><span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\">I got my make done at sephora for my engagement party and it came out fabulous. They charge you $70 ($50 if you don't want air brushing) but you get a makeover and a gift card for $70 so you can buy the products that they use on you that day. I thinking about purchasing the air brushing machine that they used on me, its $200 but it makes your skin and complexion look flawless. This is defiantly a must have item if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re doing your make up on your own on your wedding day. I'm still deciding if I'm going to do my make up myself or have it done in Jamaica. \u00a0<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"><span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif\">Good luck ladies, hope this info helps. <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" height=\"18\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheers.gif\" title=\"\" width=\"24\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"deangelis2be@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1283828960,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232103.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"DeAngelis2be","Id":232103,"Name":"DeAngelis2be","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3870d36dd27bfbd97abd4f7dc3c7e330","RawContent":"so ReeRee, how did the make up turn out.  I went to Sephora and they tried to sell me the Temptu but I couldn&#039;t justify spending the $$ for it, plus I cant think that i could use an airbrush on myself and it turn out right!!!  I finally gave up after 3 different eye trials and said fine, I just didn&#039;t buy the eye products or the temptu!!  I will go back to MAC for an eye makeover!\n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]ReeRee[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I am doing my own makeup too!  Like Rosieposie said, no one knows your face better than you and I am asian also and I just do not trust a resort makeup artist.  \n   \n So I did spent fortune on makeup products... Starting from buying Temptu Airbrushing Device from Sephora.... I kind of rationalized that that was also a birthday gift to myself....:)  I also went to MAC and bought a couple brushes, eye shadows, etc.   My wedding is about a week away and I still have to do some practice run before I leave on Wednesday!![\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1296866,"PostDate":1285478540,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <br \/> so ReeRee, how did the make up turn out.\u00a0 I went to Sephora and they tried to sell me the Temptu but I couldn't justify spending the $$ for it, plus I cant think that i could use an airbrush on myself and it turn out right!!!\u00a0 I finally gave up after 3 different eye trials and said fine, I just didn't buy the eye products or the temptu!!\u00a0 I will go back to MAC for an eye makeover!<br \/> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>ReeRee<\/strong>\u00a0<a href='\/forum\/thread\/63963\/doing-your-own-bridal-make-up#post_1433090' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid\" \/><\/span><\/a><br \/> <br \/> <p> I am doing my own makeup too!\u00a0 Like Rosieposie said, no one knows your face better than you and I am asian also and I just do not trust a resort makeup artist.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00c2\u00a0<\/p> <p> So\u00a0I did spent fortune on makeup products... Starting from buying Temptu Airbrushing Device from Sephora.... I kind of rationalized that that was also a birthday gift to myself....<img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0 I also went to MAC and bought a couple brushes, eye shadows, etc.\u00a0\u00a0 My wedding is about a week away and I still have to do some practice run before I leave on Wednesday!!\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"wendyjd@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"65.184.254.129","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1263747910,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-224774.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":135,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"wendyjd","Id":224774,"Name":"wendyjd","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"357f7f393e7163ab64e6bf0e5480317d","RawContent":"I agree with DeAngelis. \n \n I will be doing my own as well, but I walked into a Sephora a few weeks ago and asked for their best make-up consultant to ensure I know exactly what to do. She and I spoke and I told her what was going on and what I needed, and I&#039;ll be buying the necessary gift card and she&#039;ll be teaching me how to apply the make-up properly. Everyone swears that I already apply my make-up very well, but like many of you-- I don&#039;t want to look like the \"Misti\" that I look like every single day. I want to look and feel special, but I do not want to have an excess of make-up on my face... If that makes any sense.\n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]DeAngelis2be[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n [size=3]I [color=black][font=arial]would highly recommend going for a makeover at one of your favorite make up counters at a department store or at sephora. You can ask them to explain the techniques that they are using to give you the exact look. Every time I go and buy make up I learn a new tip. [\/font][\/color][\/size]You can even bring magazine print outs of looks that you&#039;re going for. \n  \n [size=3][color=black][font=arial]I got my make done at sephora for my engagement party and it came out fabulous. They charge you $70 ($50 if you don&#039;t want air brushing) but you get a makeover and a gift card for $70 so you can buy the products that they use on you that day. I thinking about purchasing the air brushing machine that they used on me, its $200 but it makes your skin and complexion look flawless. This is defiantly a must have item if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re doing your make up on your own on your wedding day. I&#039;m still deciding if I&#039;m going to do my make up myself or have it done in Jamaica.  [\/font][\/color][\/size] \n \n [size=3][color=black][font=arial]Good luck ladies, hope this info helps. [img]http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheers.gif[\/img][\/font][\/color][\/size][\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1303283,"PostDate":1286157284,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I agree with DeAngelis.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I will be doing my own as well, but I walked into a Sephora a few weeks ago and asked for their best make-up consultant to ensure I know exactly what to do. She and I spoke and I told her what was going on and what I needed, and I'll be buying the necessary gift card and she'll be teaching me how to apply the make-up properly. Everyone swears that I already apply my make-up very well, but like many of you-- I don't want to look like the \"Misti\" that I look like every single day. I want to look and feel special, but I do not want to have an excess of make-up on my face... If that makes any sense.<br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>DeAngelis2be<\/strong>\u00a0<a href='\/forum\/thread\/63963\/doing-your-own-bridal-make-up\/10#post_1441351' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><\/a><br \/> <br \/> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\">I <span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial,sans-serif\">would highly recommend going for a makeover at one of your favorite make up counters at a department store or at sephora. You can ask them to explain the techniques that they are using to give you the exact look. Every time I go and buy make up I learn a new tip. <\/span><\/span><\/span>You can even bring magazine print outs of looks that you're going for.<\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"><span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial,sans-serif\">I got my make done at sephora for my engagement party and it came out fabulous. They charge you $70 ($50 if you don't want air brushing) but you get a makeover and a gift card for $70 so you can buy the products that they use on you that day. I thinking about purchasing the air brushing machine that they used on me, its $200 but it makes your skin and complexion look flawless. This is defiantly a must have item if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re doing your make up on your own on your wedding day. I'm still deciding if I'm going to do my make up myself or have it done in Jamaica. \u00a0<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"><span  style=\"color: black\"><span  style=\"font-family: arial,sans-serif\">Good luck ladies, hope this info helps. <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" height=\"18\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheers.gif\" title=\"\" width=\"24\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>**Beaches Turks & Caicos- March 12, 2011**<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"mistibuard@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1279241667,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230302.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mistibuard","Id":230302,"Name":"mistibuard","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"20b421500393d02958833e3c8448ad2e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I plan on doing my own. I got my make-up done by a &amp;quot;pro&amp;quot; at Sephora and it was awful. I mean really, really bad. I can&#039;t trust anyone else to do it. I&#039;ve spent a lot on all new make-up but I&#039;m not counting it in the wedding budget because I figure I&#039;ll use it for other things. I needed new make-up anyways. I&#039;ve had the same stuff for years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1303313,"PostDate":1286162580,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I plan on doing my own. I got my make-up done by a \"pro\" at Sephora and it was awful. I mean really, really bad. I can't trust anyone else to do it. I've spent a lot on all new make-up but I'm not counting it in the wedding budget because I figure I'll use it for other things. I needed new make-up anyways. I've had the same stuff for years.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"danavarner@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1277834058,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-229694.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Dana2","Id":229694,"Name":"Dana2","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"29bb201900073228ac8ba52e6a0e49ab","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Hi ladies,&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I just got back from my wedding and I did do my own makeup using Temptu airbrushing.   It turned out great!&amp;nbsp;I used highlighter color Bronze to use as a bronzer because&amp;nbsp;few days before my wedding I got a good tan on the beach, so the foundation color was a little too light, but the bronzer&amp;nbsp;really did the trick. &amp;nbsp;I will upload some close-up pictures when I get home tonight, but here are the list of what I used:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Face:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Temptu airbrushing system&amp;nbsp;- foundation (natural), blush (sheer berry 404), highlighter (Copper) for undereye, highlighter (Bronze) as a bronzer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; MAC pressed power for a matt finish (the make up artist at Sephora actually told me to use loose powder such as makeup foever white loose powder, but I didn&#039;t want the finish to be too white and too mat, so I used MAC pressed power.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Eye:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Urban Decay primer potion&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; MAC eyeshadows&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Loreal HIP black eyeliner in a jar (This is a great buy! Waterproof all the way!!)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; smashbox eyebrow powder&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Clinique undereye concealer&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Lash: I got eyelash extension called Eva Lash (combination of 10mm and 12 mm)&amp;nbsp;at a local salon here in DC.&amp;nbsp; It was really uncomfortable first but I got used to it after a couple days and it looked great in the picture.&amp;nbsp; I paid $59 for it, I think it&#039;s well worth it if you don&#039;t have thick eye lashes.&amp;nbsp; Much more natural looking than fake lash you put on yourself.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Lip:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Tokidoki Lip Stain&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Smashbox lip gloss&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Will add some pictures soon!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1304021,"PostDate":1286224338,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hi ladies,<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I just got back from my wedding and I did do my own makeup using Temptu airbrushing.\u00a0\u00a0 It turned out great!\u00a0I used highlighter color Bronze to use as a bronzer because\u00a0few days before my wedding I got a good tan on the beach, so the foundation color was a little too light, but the bronzer\u00a0really did the trick. \u00a0I will upload some close-up pictures when I get home tonight, but here are the list of what I used:<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Face:<\/p> <p> Temptu airbrushing system\u00a0- foundation (natural), blush (sheer berry 404), highlighter (Copper) for undereye, highlighter (Bronze) as a bronzer.\u00a0<\/p> <p> MAC pressed power for a matt finish (the make up artist at Sephora actually told me to use loose powder such as makeup foever white loose powder, but I didn't want the finish to be too white and too mat, so I used MAC pressed power.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Eye:<\/p> <p> Urban Decay primer potion<\/p> <p> MAC eyeshadows<\/p> <p> Loreal HIP black eyeliner in a jar (This is a great buy! Waterproof all the way!!)<\/p> <p> smashbox eyebrow powder<\/p> <p> Clinique undereye concealer<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Lash: I got eyelash extension called Eva Lash (combination of 10mm and 12 mm)\u00a0at a local salon here in DC.\u00a0 It was really uncomfortable first but I got used to it after a couple days and it looked great in the picture.\u00a0 I paid $59 for it, I think it's well worth it if you don't have thick eye lashes.\u00a0 Much more natural looking than fake lash you put on yourself.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Lip:<\/p> <p> Tokidoki Lip Stain<\/p> <p> Smashbox lip gloss<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Will add some pictures soon!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lovejones312@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1269563885,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-226792.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ReeRee","Id":226792,"Name":"ReeRee","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":56749,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2cde478ffd187e8724050040d07dcb70","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I just got married last month in Dominican Republic and I did my own makeup. I got a free professional makeup appointment at Shoppers Drugmart because I spent over $75 on their makeup products (mostly Dior and Lancome).&amp;nbsp;The makeup looked great and stayed on the whole time. Plus, you get to keep the makeup which you can keep using for a long time!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I couldnt take the risk of having my makeup done at the resort spa; Ive read too many scary stories about the products and techniques they use!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Here is a pic of my face...hopefully you can get an idea of what my makeup looked like on my wedding day. I like the more heavier makeup look so it depends on the person...other like the more natural look!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"img-124.JPG\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/166219\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; xoxo Bee&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1304106,"PostDate":1286230098,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I just got married last month in Dominican Republic and I did my own makeup. I got a free professional makeup appointment at Shoppers Drugmart because I spent over $75 on their makeup products (mostly Dior and Lancome).\u00a0The makeup looked great and stayed on the whole time. Plus, you get to keep the makeup which you can keep using for a long time!<\/p> <p> I couldnt take the risk of having my makeup done at the resort spa; Ive read too many scary stories about the products and techniques they use!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Here is a pic of my face...hopefully you can get an idea of what my makeup looked like on my wedding day. I like the more heavier makeup look so it depends on the person...other like the more natural look!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/166219\/width\/1000\/height\/800' class='bbc_url' title=''><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"img-124.JPG\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/166219\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> xoxo Bee<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Married @ Dreams La Romana, Dominican Republic September 10th 2010<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"10weddingbells@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1269560884,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-226789.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":133,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Pink_Petals","Id":226789,"Name":"Pink_Petals","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":41,"TotalPages":5,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":40},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
